cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Streaming inversion-free quasi-Newton estimation and inference on dependent data"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, and cite the accompanying paper."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kendiukhov
    given-names: Ihor
    email: ihor.kendiukhov@student.uni-tuebingen.de
    affiliation: "Institute of Medical Genetics and Applied Genomics, University of Tübingen"
version: release1
date-released: "2026-08-11"
# Concept DOI: always resolves to the most recent release.  The DOI of this particular
# release is 10.5281/zenodo.21891313.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21891312
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kendiukhov/streaming-quasi-newton-dependent-data"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of BGSN (blocked-gapped streaming Newton): a single-pass,
  O(dN)-time, O(d^2)-memory quasi-Newton estimator whose confidence intervals remain
  valid on temporally dependent data streams, together with the full experimental
  pipeline of the accompanying paper.
license: MIT
keywords:
  - stochastic approximation
  - streaming inference
  - quasi-Newton
  - long-run variance
  - HAC covariance
  - mixing processes
